{%- comment -%}
  TEMPORARY — delete this snippet (and its render in layout/theme.liquid) once
  the sa-booking-admin extension has been redeployed.

  THE BUG (live, found 2026-08-30): in the booking widget's app block,
  `selectedCalDate` is declared with `var` INSIDE renderClass(), but
  renderDiscountNudge() sits one scope up and reads it. So every click on a
  date in single-session mode threw

      ReferenceError: selectedCalDate is not defined

  and the throw landed BEFORE updateUI() — which is what writes the price, the
  total and enables "Add to Cart". Picking a date left all three blank and the
  button disabled, so no class or workshop could actually be booked. Verified
  with the widget in its original inline position too, so it is the app's bug,
  not the booking modal's.

  THE REAL FIX is one line in the extension:
  extensions/booking-embed/blocks/booking-widget.liquid — declare
  `var selectedCalDate = null;` beside `selectedDates` at widget scope and
  leave a bare assignment where the old declaration was. It is already made in
  the admin repo, waiting on a deploy; the Shopify CLI cannot reach the partner
  org from this machine, so it cannot be shipped from here.

  THE SHIM: declaring the name at global scope gives that free variable
  something to resolve to, so the read returns null instead of throwing and
  updateUI() runs. The widget's own `var` inside renderClass still shadows it,
  so the real single-mode date logic is untouched.

  KNOWN COST: renderDiscountNudge now always sees null in single-session mode,
  so the "Also available: Full term …" nudge does not appear when a single date
  is picked. Multi-date mode reads selectedDates and still shows it in full.
  The deploy of the real fix restores it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  var selectedCalDate = null;
</script>
